---
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = '3 November 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — sur9e"
  description="What sur9e.com collects (almost nothing), what it does not, and how to get your data removed."
>
  <main id="main" class="pp">
    <article class="pp-wrap">
      <a class="pp-back" href="/">← sur9e</a>

      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="pp-lede">
        This page covers <strong>this website</strong> (sur9e.com). The app itself
        runs on your machine and is a separate story: it talks to no sur9e server,
        because there isn't one.
      </p>

      <p class="pp-callout">
        No analytics. No cookies. No tracking pixels. No ads. Fonts and images
        are served from this domain, not from Google.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>The email you type into the release-notes form.</strong> It is posted
          to a small worker we run, stored so we can send you occasional release notes,
          and used for nothing else. There is no account attached to it and no profile
          built around it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email you send us.</strong> Messages to
          <a href="mailto:hello@sur9e.com">hello@sur9e.com</a> arrive in a normal
          inbox and stay there while we deal with them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Standard request logs at our host.</strong> Cloudflare processes
          what any web server processes to serve a page and stop abuse — IP address,
          user agent, timestamp — under its own retention policy. We don't build anything
          from it.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No third-party scripts on any page.</li>
        <li>
          No cookies set by this site, no local storage tracking, no
          fingerprinting.
        </li>
        <li>
          No account, payment, or profile data — there is nothing to sign into.
        </li>
        <li>
          We don't sell, rent, or share your data with advertisers or data
          brokers.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How to get out</h2>
      <p>
        Reply to any release-notes email, or write to
        <a href="mailto:hello@sur9e.com">hello@sur9e.com</a>, and we'll delete
        the address. The same address works for asking what we hold about you.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        If you're in the EEA or UK (GDPR) or California (CCPA/CPRA), you can ask
        to access, correct, or delete the personal data we hold about you, and
        we won't treat you differently for asking. In practice that data is an
        email address you gave us, or a message you sent — nothing more.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site isn't directed at children under 13, and we don't knowingly
        collect their data.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this ever changes in a way that matters, this page changes first and
        the date below moves with it.
      </p>

      <p class="pp-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="mailto:hello@sur9e.com">hello@sur9e.com</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .pp {
    min-height: 100vh;
    background: var(--paper, #faf9f6);
    color: var(--ink, #14100d);
    padding: 88px 24px 96px;
  }

  .pp-wrap {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .pp-back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .pp-back:hover {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(34px, 6vw, 48px);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 19px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 40px 0 10px;
  }

  .pp-lede {
    font-size: 18px;
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  .pp-callout {
    border-left: 3px solid currentColor;
    padding: 4px 0 4px 16px;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  ul {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    padding-left: 20px;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  a {
    color: inherit;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .pp-updated {
    margin-top: 28px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.55;
  }
</style>
